ng>PWABuilder</strong> Microsoft ka ek free online tool hai — <a href="https://pwabuilder.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-orange-600 hover:text-orange-700 dark:text-orange-400 dark:hover:text-orange-300 underline">pwabuilder.com</a>.</p>
<p dir="auto" class="my-3 leading-[25px]"><strong>Kaam:</strong> Aapka website/web app (jo PWA-compatible hai, jaise humara Artikaz app) usse lekar wo ek <strong>asli Android APK</strong> bana deta hai. Matlab wahi app jo browser me chalta tha, wo ek installable Android app ban jata hai jise kisi bhi phone par seedha install kar sakte hain.</p>
<p dir="auto" class="my-3 leading-[25px]"><strong>Kaise kaam karta hai:</strong></p>
<ol dir="auto" class="my-2 ps-7 list-decimal">
<li dir="auto" class="my-1 leading-[25px]">Apne hosted app ka URL paste karte hain (GitHub Pages wala link).</li>
<li dir="auto" class="my-1 leading-[25px]">Ye app ko analyze karta hai aur batata hai sab kuch theek hai ya nahi.</li>
<li dir="auto" class="my-1 leading-[25px]">"Android" package download karne ka option deta hai — APK ya AAB (Play Store ke liye) file mil jati hai.</li>
